    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW26wAfLRRbhSQHUmjT3byNkC)_\n\nCleans up plain-BibTeX handling in the academic modules (`sp-academic.org` is canonical; the `.el` files were tangled from it).\n\n**Citation keys: `smithjones-2017-atten-all`.** Your settings: year length 4, `-` between name, year and title words, 2 title words (stretch 1) of at most 5 letters. Your later edit in the `.el` (first two authors, ignore list gains \"Is\", \"the\", \"a\") is kept and the doc now matches it; \"On\" and \"on\" are also ignored; keys are lower case and ASCII (`Müller` → `muller`). Before, the options were set twice with different values and `biblio` entries kept whatever the service returned. Now:\n- all `bibtex-autokey-*` options live in one `use-package bibtex` block in `sp-bibprocess`;\n- `biblio-bibtex-use-autokey` gives inserted entries the same key;\n- `bibtex-search-entry-globally` + `bibtex-files` check keys across all registered files.\n\n**One folder option.** `sp-bibliography-dir` (in `sp-paths`) is the only one and now defaults to `~/Documents/bibliography`. `sp-bibtex-dir` (a copy of it) and the unused `sp-bibliography` are removed, no aliases. `sp-org-export` read `sp-bibliography` for pandoc; `sp-cite-to-org` / `sp-cite-to-markdown` now pass one `--bibliography` flag per registered `.bib` file. Existing `.bib` files must move to the new folder (or set `SP_BIBLIOGRAPHY_DIR`).\n\n**One bibliography list.** `sp-bibtex-register` also sets `org-ref-default-bibliography`, `bibtex-completion-bibliography` and `bibtex-files` (previously a hard-coded list of seven files in `sp-academic`, `master.bib` only for org-ref). The file regexp is fixed.\n\n**Citar fixes** (both were bugs):\n- `citar-bibliography` / `org-cite-global-bibliography` were set from `sp-bibliography` (nil), so Citar loaded with an empty bibliography. They now use `sp-bibtex-files`.\n- `citar-library-paths` was commented out; it is now `sp-literature-dir`. The extensions and separator moved to `sp-citations`; the `(setq citar-library-file-extensions nil)` it overrode is gone.\n- The `citar-symbols` `when` form and the `citar-notes-paths` `setq` sat inside `:custom` and never applied; they moved to `:config` / a proper entry (notes path falls back to `sp-notes-dir`).\n\n**Also:** removed the verbatim repeated block in `sp-bibprocess`; the `defcustom`s in `sp-academic` come before the `require`s; `citar-org-node` uses an Elpaca recipe instead of `:vc`; `H-b` moved into the `bibtex` block. The doc has \"Citation keys\" and \"Settings worth knowing\" sections.\n\n**Checked** (Emacs 29.3, batch): the key function (`smithjones-2017-atten-all`, `hegel-1807-phanom-geist`, `mullerjones-2020-origin-species`); `sp-bibtex-register` and `sp--pandoc-bibliography-args` on a temp directory; the edited files read without errors; docs tangle to the `.el` byte for byte (own tangler). `tools/set-defcustom-group.py --check` only reports `sp-collection-query-tables*.el`, which this PR does not touch. **Not run:** the whole configuration, Citar/org-cite with real `.bib` files, `biblio` insertion, pandoc, the Elpaca recipe for `citar-org-node`.\n\n**Overlap:** #87 also moves the three `defcustom`s to the top of `sp-academic` and will conflict in that hunk.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01HNdCfPPQBnsznsDyobvCof\n",
