                "message": "Normalise BibTeX keys and register one list of .bib files\n\n- One citation-key scheme (smith2020attention), set once in sp-bibprocess\n  with ASCII folding; biblio entries use it too.\n- sp-bibtex-register feeds org-cite, citar, org-ref, helm-bibtex and\n  bibtex-files from the same list; bibtex searches keys globally.\n- citar: library paths, extensions and notes path applied; icons moved\n  out of :custom; the obsolete sp-bibliography no longer empties the\n  bibliography.\n- Remove the repeated definitions in sp-bibprocess and the duplicated\n  autokey blocks in sp-academic; citar-org-node via Elpaca recipe.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HNdCfPPQBnsznsDyobvCof",
                "tree": {
                    "sha": "c29d8ea08655265f248e38dd228f1267f69c4879",
                    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/siainbuletin/dotfiles/git/trees/c29d8ea08655265f248e38dd228f1267f69c4879"
